Installed aide via dnf, initialized the database against the distro-default config (which explicitly covers ~100 critical /etc paths plus a catch-all /etc PERMS rule), activated it as /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz, and validated detection by modifying and reverting /etc/issue (AIDE correctly reported the change with exit code 4 and exact hash/size diffs, then reported clean after revert). Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id and a clean AIDE check, issued `systemctl reboot` with the ack returning before disconnect, polled until node1 was reachable again, confirmed the boot_id changed, and verified the AIDE database and integrity check both survived and remain functional post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (AlmaLinux 9.6) and confirmed dnf availability\",\"Installed aide package via dnf\",\"Reviewed /etc/aide.conf default rules confirming comprehensive /etc coverage\",\"Ran aide --init to build the baseline database (28662 entries)\",\"Activated the baseline by moving aide.db.new.gz to aide.db.gz\",\"Ran aide --check confirming a clean baseline (no differences)\",\"Modified /etc/issue, re-ran aide --check to prove change detection (exit 4, diff details shown), then reverted the file and confirmed clean state again\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and AIDE db checksum as baseline\",\"Issued a backgrounded systemctl reboot on node1 so the ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed, indicating an actual restart\",\"Re-verified AIDE db checksum unchanged and aide --check still reports a clean /etc baseline post-restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"AIDE installed and integrity baseline database initialized for /etc\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3ff0c3f0d14e4859\",\"cmd-0f02218fea9d473e\",\"cmd-d38fb0c0e1104a38\",\"cmd-8556d08ea68e40c0\",\"cmd-2d1b88f14239464d\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed AlmaLinux 9 with dnf, installed aide, reviewed default config's extensive /etc coverage, and ran aide --init producing a 28662-entry database in ~5s.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline database activated and confirmed clean against current /etc state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d17200128ff84c5c\",\"cmd-f6963127620c433f\"],\"summary\":\"Moved aide.db.new.gz to aide.db.gz and ran aide --check, which reported 'NO differences between database and filesystem'.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline proven functional by detecting a real change to /etc and confirming revert restores clean state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1d32082301264bb9\",\"cmd-ea2478ff248d4617\"],\"summary\":\"Appended a line to /etc/issue; aide --check exited 4 and reported the exact file, size change (23->47 bytes), and hash diffs. After reverting /etc/issue, aide --check again reported no differences.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy pre-restart baseline captured on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a987eaf0c6f445a2\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 82d4f0d1-b4b2-494f-8b25-851ee6e6dec7, boot time, and md5 of the AIDE database prior to restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-61b14f8ca0764080\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'sleep 2 && systemctl reboot' returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately, before the node disconnected.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart proven via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ce7e1be76cd149c2\",\"cmd-dcd31a941f16451a\",\"cmd-cc5744f7e1254b52\"],\"summary\":\"Connection reset was observed mid-reboot (cmd-dcd31a941f16451a), then polling succeeded with a new boot_id 0659a87b-24ff-4f3b-8b14-bd054391a4f6, differing from the pre-restart boot_id, confirming an actual reboot occurred.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of the integrity baseline verified\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fcc7750170104284\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, the AIDE database md5 (9f02adc21b5c85aca11215df2c3d8e95) matched the pre-restart checksum, and aide --check again reported 'NO differences', confirming the baseline and its checking capability persisted through the reboot.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Established an AIDE-based file integrity baseline for /etc on node1 (AlmaLinux 9). Installed aide via dnf, initialized the database against the distro-default config (which explicitly covers ~100 critical /etc paths plus a catch-all /etc PERMS rule), activated it as /var/lib/aide/aide.db.gz, and validated detection by modifying and reverting /etc/issue (AIDE correctly reported the change with exit code 4 and exact hash/size diffs, then reported clean after revert). Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id and a clean AIDE check, issued `systemctl reboot` with the ack returning before disconnect, polled until node1 was reachable again, confirmed the boot_id changed, and verified the AIDE database and integrity check both survived and remain functional post-restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS (AlmaLinux 9.6) and confirmed dnf availability","Installed aide package via dnf","Reviewed /etc/aide.conf default rules confirming comprehensive /etc coverage","Ran aide --init to build the baseline database (28662 entries)","Activated the baseline by moving aide.db.new.gz to aide.db.gz","Ran aide --check confirming a clean baseline (no differences)","Modified /etc/issue, re-ran aide --check to prove change detection (exit 4, diff details shown), then reverted the file and confirmed clean state again","Captured pre-restart boot_id and AIDE db checksum as baseline","Issued a backgrounded systemctl reboot on node1 so the ack returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned","Confirmed boot_id changed, indicating an actual restart","Re-verified AIDE db checksum unchanged and aide --check still reports a clean /etc baseline post-restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"AIDE installed and integrity baseline database initialized for /etc","command_ids":["cmd-3ff0c3f0d14e4859","cmd-0f02218fea9d473e","cmd-d38fb0c0e1104a38","cmd-8556d08ea68e40c0","cmd-2d1b88f14239464d"],"summary":"Confirmed AlmaLinux 9 with dnf, installed aide, reviewed default config's extensive /etc coverage, and ran aide --init producing a 28662-entry database in ~5s."},{"requirement":"Baseline database activated and confirmed clean against current /etc state","command_ids":["cmd-d17200128ff84c5c","cmd-f6963127620c433f"],"summary":"Moved aide.db.new.gz to aide.db.gz and ran aide --check, which reported 'NO differences between database and filesystem'."},{"requirement":"Baseline proven functional by detecting a real change to /etc and confirming revert restores clean state","command_ids":["cmd-1d32082301264bb9","cmd-ea2478ff248d4617"],"summary":"Appended a line to /etc/issue; aide --check exited 4 and reported the exact file, size change (23->47 bytes), and hash diffs. After reverting /etc/issue, aide --check again reported no differences."},{"requirement":"Healthy pre-restart baseline captured on node1","command_ids":["cmd-a987eaf0c6f445a2"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 82d4f0d1-b4b2-494f-8b25-851ee6e6dec7, boot time, and md5 of the AIDE database prior to restart."},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-61b14f8ca0764080"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'sleep 2 && systemctl reboot' returned 'reboot scheduled' immediately, before the node disconnected."},{"requirement":"node1 restart proven via changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-ce7e1be76cd149c2","cmd-dcd31a941f16451a","cmd-cc5744f7e1254b52"],"summary":"Connection reset was observed mid-reboot (cmd-dcd31a941f16451a), then polling succeeded with a new boot_id 0659a87b-24ff-4f3b-8b14-bd054391a4f6, differing from the pre-restart boot_id, confirming an actual reboot occurred."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of the integrity baseline verified","command_ids":["cmd-fcc7750170104284"],"summary":"After restart, the AIDE database md5 (9f02adc21b5c85aca11215df2c3d8e95) ma